  "term": "vitreous hemorrhage",
  "definition": "Vitreous hemorrhage is bleeding into the vitreous humor, the gel-like material inside the eye. It can happen from abnormal new blood vessel growth, a retinal tear or detachment, or rupture of an aneurysm in an eye blood vessel.",
